{{!-- First-session guide, laid out as a left-rail tabbed sheet like Run an Expedition
      and Make a Monster: the rail (shared .stonetop-guide-toc) switches which step panel
      is shown, client-side, so the single window stays short and every panel keeps its
      state. An "Overview" landing sits above the six Book I "Getting Started" steps. See
      dialogs/WelcomeDialog.js. --}}
<div class="stonetop-welcome">

  <div class="stonetop-guide-split stonetop-welcome-split">

    {{!-- Step rail (jump between the overview + the six steps; shared journal-style list). --}}
    <nav class="stonetop-guide-toc" aria-label="First-session steps">
      <ol class="stonetop-guide-toc-list">
        {{#each sections}}
        <li class="stonetop-guide-toc-item{{#if selected}} is-active{{/if}}">
          <button type="button" class="stonetop-guide-toc-btn stonetop-welcome-tab" data-tab="{{key}}"{{#if selected}} aria-current="true"{{/if}}>
            <i class="fas {{icon}} stonetop-guide-toc-icon"></i>
            <span class="stonetop-guide-toc-text">{{title}}</span>
          </button>
        </li>
        {{/each}}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="stonetop-guide-main stonetop-welcome-main">

      {{!-- Banner: the active step's icon + title + count (updated in JS on tab switch,
            so panels never re-render and keep their in-progress state). --}}
      <div class="stonetop-guide-banner stonetop-welcome-banner">
        <i class="fas {{active.icon}} stonetop-guide-banner-icon stonetop-welcome-banner-icon"></i>
        <div class="stonetop-guide-banner-info">
          <div class="stonetop-welcome-banner-titlewrap">
            <span class="stonetop-guide-banner-title stonetop-welcome-banner-title">{{active.title}}</span>
            <span class="stonetop-welcome-banner-optional"{{#unless active.optional}} hidden{{/unless}}>optional</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stonetop-guide-banner-sub">First-session guide</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stonetop-guide-count stonetop-welcome-banner-count"{{#unless active.count}} hidden{{/unless}}>{{active.count}}</div>
      </div>

      {{!-- Overview / landing --}}
      <section class="stonetop-welcome-section" data-tab="overview"{{#unless (eq activeTab "overview")}} hidden{{/unless}}>
        <header class="stonetop-welcome-hero">
          <h2>Welcome to <span class="stonetop-welcome-logo">Stonetop</span>!</h2>
        </header>

        <p class="stonetop-welcome-lead">{{{premiseHtml}}}</p>

        <p class="stonetop-welcome-intro">
          The first session is mostly about building the village and its heroes together. Work through these steps as a group; there are no wrong answers, only the world you make.
        </p>

        <p class="stonetop-welcome-newbie">
          Never run a game in Foundry before?
          <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-textlink stonetop-welcome-textlink--inline" data-action="foundry-basics">
            <i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i> New to Foundry?
          </button>
        </p>

        <div class="stonetop-welcome-outro">
          <p>Not sure where to start? Open the <strong>Setting Overview</strong> and read it through together: the rest of the session grows from there. You can reopen this guide any time from the <span class="stonetop-welcome-springicon-wrap stonetop-welcome-springicon-wrap--signpost"><img class="stonetop-welcome-springicon" src="systems/stonetop-pwd/assets/icons/macros/direction-signs.svg" alt=""></span> <em>signpost</em> icon in your hotbar below.</p>
          <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-action" data-action="setting-overview">
            <i class="fas fa-book-open"></i> Open Setting Overview
          </button>
        </div>
      </section>

      {{!-- Step 1: import book art --}}
      <section class="stonetop-welcome-section" data-tab="book-art"{{#unless (eq activeTab "book-art")}} hidden{{/unless}}>
        <p>If you own the Stonetop PDFs, you can rebuild the monster and location illustrations right here in your world: portraits, tokens, and journal art all filled in from your own books. Nothing is uploaded anywhere; the pictures are reconstructed locally on your machine.</p>
        <p>The same window turns the five poster maps you own into ready-to-use Scenes, from either the separate map images or the single all-maps PDF. You can do that on its own, without supplying a book.</p>
        {{#if bookArtImported}}
          <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice stonetop-welcome-notice--done">
            <i class="fas fa-circle-check"></i>
            <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice-body">
              <span><strong>Already done: nothing to do here.</strong> Your imported art is kept outside the world, so this world found it and wired it in by itself. You do <strong>not</strong> need your PDFs again. Re-run the import below only if you want art that a newer version of Stonetop added.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        {{/if}}
        <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-action" data-action="import-book-art">
          <i class="fas fa-images"></i> {{#if bookArtImported}}Import Book Art Again{{else}}Import Book Art{{/if}}
        </button>
        {{!-- Shown only when there is something to build. A newer version of Stonetop can add
              pictures that are derivable from art already on disk — individual faces cut out of
              a group scene, and the square close-ups the small round portraits use — so these
              need no PDFs and no re-import. Normally offered once by a chat card; here as well,
              because that card is easy to miss and never comes back. --}}
        {{#if rebuildableArt}}
        <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-action" data-action="rebuild-portraits">
          <i class="fas fa-crop-simple"></i> Build {{rebuildableArt}} more portraits from art you already have
        </button>
        {{/if}}
        <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice stonetop-welcome-notice--info">
          <i class="fas fa-circle-info"></i>
          <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice-body">
            <span>You'll be asked for your <strong>Book I</strong> and/or <strong>Book II</strong> &ldquo;spreads&rdquo; PDFs (provide either or both), and optionally the free <strong>GM playbook</strong> PDF, which holds the sharpest copies of the three regional maps and the only copies of the core-loop and flow-of-play diagrams. It's best to run this <strong>before your players join</strong> for the first session, and to <strong>close any journal you're editing</strong> first so your in-progress edits don't collide with the art (it only adds pictures; it never overwrites your or your players' text). You can re-run it any time from the <strong>Import Book Art</strong> macro in your Macro Directory.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {{!-- Step 2: review the setting --}}
      <section class="stonetop-welcome-section" data-tab="setting"{{#unless (eq activeTab "setting")}} hidden{{/unless}}>
        <p>Open the Setting Overview together and give everyone 10&ndash;15 minutes with it, then field questions. Some things (like &ldquo;where did the Forest Folk go?&rdquo;) are mysteries to discover in play.</p>
        <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-action" data-action="setting-overview">
          <i class="fas fa-book-open"></i> Open Setting Overview
        </button>
      </section>

      {{!-- Step 3: set expectations --}}
      <section class="stonetop-welcome-section" data-tab="expectations"{{#unless (eq activeTab "expectations")}} hidden{{/unless}}>
        <p>Share the players' agenda and principles (the Setting Overview's <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-textlink stonetop-welcome-textlink--inline" data-action="agenda-principles">Agenda &amp; Principles</button> tab), and talk through any content to exclude, veil, or handle with care.</p>
      </section>

      {{!-- Step 4: create characters --}}
      <section class="stonetop-welcome-section" data-tab="characters"{{#unless (eq activeTab "characters")}} hidden{{/unless}}>
        <p>Make characters together. Start one for each player below: it opens on their screen with a big <strong>Create Character</strong> button that walks them through choosing a playbook and filling it in. Wait until everyone has completed their character before moving on to the next step. You can find answers to common questions in the Setting Overview.</p>

        {{#if noPlayers}}
        <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice stonetop-welcome-notice--warn">
          <i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
          <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice-body">
            <span>No players have joined this world yet. Add them in Foundry's <strong>Configure Players</strong> screen.</span>
            <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-action" data-action="configure-players" title="Opens Foundry's player management page (you'll leave the game and can return when you're done)">
              <i class="fas fa-users-cog"></i> Configure Players
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        {{else}}
        <ul class="stonetop-welcome-players">
          {{#each players}}
          <li class="stonetop-welcome-player">
            <span class="stonetop-welcome-player-status {{#if active}}is-online{{else}}is-offline{{/if}}" title="{{#if active}}Online{{else}}Offline{{/if}}"></span>
            <img class="stonetop-welcome-player-avatar" src="{{avatar}}" alt="">
            <div class="stonetop-welcome-player-info">
              <span class="stonetop-welcome-player-name" style="color: {{color}};">{{name}}</span>
              {{#if characters.length}}
              <span class="stonetop-welcome-player-has">
                has
                {{#each characters}}<span class="stonetop-welcome-player-entry"><a class="stonetop-welcome-player-char" data-actor-id="{{id}}" title="Open this character sheet">{{name}}</a>{{#if progress.playbook}}<span class="stonetop-welcome-player-playbook" title="Selected playbook">{{progress.playbook}}</span>{{/if}}{{#if progress}}<span class="stonetop-welcome-player-progress stonetop-welcome-player-progress--{{progress.status}}" title="Character creation progress">{{progress.text}}</span>{{/if}}</span>{{/each}}
              </span>
              {{/if}}
            </div>
            {{!-- Not styled as destructive for a player who already has one: the button now
                  asks whether the new character joins theirs or replaces it, and only the
                  second answer deletes anything. --}}
            <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-create" data-user-id="{{id}}">
              <i class="fas fa-user-plus"></i> {{#if characters.length}}Another Character{{else}}Create Character{{/if}}
            </button>
          </li>
          {{/each}}
        </ul>
        {{/if}}
      </section>

      {{!-- Step 5: introduce the PCs --}}
      <section class="stonetop-welcome-section" data-tab="introduce"{{#unless (eq activeTab "introduce")}} hidden{{/unless}}>
        <p>Once the sheets are built, go around the table: introduce yourselves, add details, and ask &amp; answer questions about each other and Stonetop. The guided Introductions walk you through it round by round, ending as you add each character's home to the steading and <em>let spring break forth</em>.</p>
        <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-action" data-action="introductions">
          <i class="fas fa-users"></i> Start Introductions
        </button>
        <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice stonetop-welcome-notice--info">
          <i class="fas fa-feather"></i>
          <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice-body">
            <span>The GM records each answer along the way, here and in the <em>Let Spring Burst Forth</em> walkthrough, and finishing each compiles them into a <strong>Player Introductions</strong> journal, kept in a folder named <strong>The Chronicle</strong> and readable by the whole table, so you can look back on them all campaign long.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {{!-- Step 6: let spring burst forth --}}
      <section class="stonetop-welcome-section" data-tab="spring"{{#unless (eq activeTab "spring")}} hidden{{/unless}}>
        <p>Once the Introductions wrap up with <em>let spring break forth</em>, walk through <strong>Let Spring Burst Forth</strong>: the most hopeful character makes the season's first <strong>Seasons Change</strong> move, and its result sets up your opening hook.</p>
        <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-action" data-action="spring-burst">
          <i class="fas fa-seedling"></i> Walk Through Let Spring Burst Forth
        </button>
        <p>Resist the urge to leap straight into adventure: take time to mull over everything your players gave you, and prepare the first expedition.</p>
        <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice stonetop-welcome-notice--info">
          <i class="fas fa-rotate-right"></i>
          <div class="stonetop-welcome-notice-body">
            <span>Every season after this one, make the <strong>Seasons Change</strong> move from the <span class="stonetop-welcome-springicon-wrap"><img class="stonetop-welcome-springicon" src="systems/stonetop-pwd/assets/icons/macros/spring.svg" alt=""></span> <em>Seasons Change</em> button in your hotbar below: it walks you through the roll, the seasonal gains, and the season's bookkeeping.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

  </div>

  <footer class="stonetop-guide-nav stonetop-welcome-nav">
    <label class="stonetop-welcome-dontshow">
      <input type="checkbox" class="stonetop-welcome-dontshow-input" {{#if dontShowAgain}}checked{{/if}}>
      Don't show this again
    </label>
    <span class="stonetop-welcome-nav-btns">
      <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-back"{{#if atFirst}} disabled{{/if}}><span class="stonetop-nav-arrow stonetop-nav-arrow--back"></span>Back</button>
      <button type="button" class="stonetop-welcome-next"{{#if atLast}} disabled{{/if}}>Next<span class="stonetop-nav-arrow"></span></button>
    </span>
  </footer>

</div>
